  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run it or `vite build` here, so nothing has been rendered or checked in a browser.\n\n- **Island:** flat-shaded terrain built from per-triangle vertices with face normals and height-based colours (sand, grass, rock). It has a jittered grid, an irregular shoreline and a hill. About 34 low-poly pines (a trunk and two cones each) and about 26 rocks are instanced on and around it.\n- **Water:** a large, stretched grid with a custom GLSL shader. Sine waves move the vertices. Flat-shaded facets come from screen-space derivatives. It has a Fresnel reflection of the sky colour, sun and moon glints, shallow-to-deep tint, foam on wave crests and a fade to the sky colour at distance. The sun position, sky colour and brightness are pushed to its uniforms every frame.\n- **Day/night:** a full cycle takes 20 seconds, starting at hour 9. A Preetham sky with stars is moved each frame with `app.atmosphere.setSky`. The sun and moon directional lights move on arcs. The sun's intensity and colour change from warm at the horizon to white at noon and fade to zero at night. The moon and the hemisphere light keep the scene lit at night, and a neutral environment adds a little fill.\n- **Camera:** a perspective camera about 40 units from the island and 12 above the water, with a field of view of 55°. It swings back and forth (about ±30°) around the island through `app.camera?.setPose`. The framing leaves a strip of sky visible above the horizon.\n- **Startup:** everything is inside an async `main()` because Vite's default build target rejects top-level await. After `app.ready()` it sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` in the next `requestAnimationFrame`.\n\nBecause it was never run, these points are unverified:\n- whether the sky colour matches the water's far fade;\n- the tree and rock placement on the faceted terrain;\n- whether `setPose` overrides the camera declared in the scene.\n\n",
